WEBVTT

00:00:32.490 --> 00:00:33.990
Did you hear?

00:00:34.070 --> 00:00:34.780
About what?

00:00:34.910 --> 00:00:37.120
The new student.

00:00:37.660 --> 00:00:39.370
New student?

00:00:59.050 --> 00:01:00.810
<i>The wind is sweet.</i>

00:01:01.520 --> 00:01:04.270
<i>The air has a scent.</i>

00:01:07.190 --> 00:01:10.360
<i>So this is Earth.</i>

00:01:39.800 --> 00:01:40.640
Hi.

00:01:43.970 --> 00:01:46.600
<i>Sunny with scattered cherry blossoms.</i>

00:01:47.730 --> 00:01:51.570
<i>It was the day I first met
Ryoichi Kyogoku.</i>

00:01:55.480 --> 00:02:03.030
PSYCHIC SCHOOL WARS

00:02:28.270 --> 00:02:30.400
Original Novel by Taku Mayumura

00:02:34.980 --> 00:02:39.320
<i>The day I met Kyogoku,
two things happened.</i>

00:02:40.530 --> 00:02:43.330
<i>It was sunny as usual.</i>

00:02:43.910 --> 00:02:47.580
<i>A windy morning as usual.</i>

00:02:50.710 --> 00:02:52.830
You're here every morning.

00:02:53.710 --> 00:02:56.550
It's nice you walk
him every day.

00:02:56.670 --> 00:02:59.170
Yeah... It's my job.

00:02:59.630 --> 00:03:00.800
Name?

00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:04.680
Seki... Kenji Seki.

00:03:05.180 --> 00:03:07.680
Not you. The dog.

00:03:08.270 --> 00:03:11.940
I know your name.
Same class this year.

00:03:14.820 --> 00:03:18.240
His name is Shiro
for “white.”

00:03:18.650 --> 00:03:20.650
Good morning, Shiro.

00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:27.660
<i>I had a conversation with
class rep Kahori Harukawa.</i>

00:03:28.160 --> 00:03:32.040
<i>Definitely, this year's
number one incident!</i>

00:03:32.210 --> 00:03:34.040
Shiro, good job!

00:03:34.170 --> 00:03:35.920
Today is the luckiest...

00:03:36.040 --> 00:03:37.090
You pervert!

00:03:37.210 --> 00:03:37.840
What?

00:03:37.920 --> 00:03:40.590
You were staring at Kahori.

00:03:40.720 --> 00:03:43.260
That obscene look
in your eyes...

00:03:43.390 --> 00:03:45.510
I was not staring at her.

00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:47.060
Yes, you were.

00:03:47.140 --> 00:03:48.810
Officer, a pervert!

00:03:48.890 --> 00:03:51.390
- Stop it!
- Help!

00:03:52.230 --> 00:03:53.060
Officer!

00:03:53.190 --> 00:03:55.360
Natsuki, stop it!

00:03:57.270 --> 00:03:58.230
Ouch...

00:03:58.320 --> 00:03:59.570
Pervert.

00:04:00.280 --> 00:04:01.240
But you were...

00:04:01.320 --> 00:04:03.820
But look.

00:04:05.990 --> 00:04:07.410
Since when?

00:04:08.030 --> 00:04:09.370
Since the beginning.

00:04:09.450 --> 00:04:10.580
All the time?

00:04:10.660 --> 00:04:11.710
All the time.

00:04:11.790 --> 00:04:15.290
Kaho must have seen it too.
How could she not?

00:04:16.380 --> 00:04:18.460
My life is over.

00:04:19.800 --> 00:04:25.090
<i>The other incident was this fatal
mishap and having it witnessed</i>

00:04:25.180 --> 00:04:28.430
<i>by her, Natsuki Suzuura.</i>

00:04:28.560 --> 00:04:31.730
<i>If she tells everyone at school...</i>

00:04:31.930 --> 00:04:36.770
Your fly... Your nickname as of
today is Mr. Open Fly.

00:04:37.610 --> 00:04:41.860
<i>Definitely, today is the
worst day of my life.</i>

00:04:42.900 --> 00:04:43.740
Him.

00:04:43.820 --> 00:04:44.610
Please!

00:04:44.740 --> 00:04:46.490
Hey, you!

00:04:48.410 --> 00:04:51.330
<i>But the truly major incident</i>

00:04:51.580 --> 00:04:55.670
<i>was already in progress
when I met Kyogoku.</i>

00:04:57.420 --> 00:05:02.420
<i>Even though, I didn't realize
until much later.</i>

00:05:03.590 --> 00:05:04.930
Kaho!

00:05:05.130 --> 00:05:06.930
You went surfing
this morning.

00:05:07.010 --> 00:05:08.300
You saw me?

00:05:08.390 --> 00:05:10.680
Yeah. It's my jogging course.

00:05:11.600 --> 00:05:16.980
Starting this year, mobile phones
will not be permitted on campus.

00:05:17.060 --> 00:05:21.320
Please inform your students
about this new rule.

00:05:21.400 --> 00:05:24.990
Take a seat.
I'll be with you soon.

00:05:25.110 --> 00:05:26.200
Sure.

00:05:27.610 --> 00:05:29.530
I saw Kenji this morning too.

00:05:30.700 --> 00:05:32.700
He was walking Shiro.

00:05:32.830 --> 00:05:35.330
He used to go at night.

00:05:35.460 --> 00:05:38.460
But for some reason,
he wakes up early now.

00:05:39.790 --> 00:05:40.960
What's the matter?

00:05:41.040 --> 00:05:42.090
Nothing.

00:05:42.170 --> 00:05:45.840
Did he sexually harass you
or something?

00:05:45.970 --> 00:05:48.220
I didn't say anything.

00:05:48.340 --> 00:05:52.510
Well... What happened?
What? What? Tell me.

00:05:52.810 --> 00:05:54.350
About what?!

00:06:11.030 --> 00:06:13.990
Hot!

00:06:23.840 --> 00:06:27.170
I can't believe this.
No mobile phones?

00:06:27.260 --> 00:06:30.890
Parents and teachers only
think of themselves.

00:06:31.050 --> 00:06:33.010
This is insane.

00:06:33.100 --> 00:06:36.220
But it's no surprise
after what happened...

00:06:38.020 --> 00:06:40.190
I wonder if Yamagiwa
will show up.

00:06:40.270 --> 00:06:44.570
She's in your club, right?
There were lots of rumors.

00:06:44.690 --> 00:06:47.190
It sucks to flunk second year.

00:06:47.280 --> 00:06:49.110
I'd refuse to come
to school.

00:06:49.240 --> 00:06:51.910
You use a mobile too.

00:06:51.990 --> 00:06:53.490
Yeah but...

00:06:53.580 --> 00:06:55.580
The student council approved.

00:06:55.700 --> 00:06:57.080
Unbelievable.

00:06:57.620 --> 00:07:01.960
People who don't have one don't
understand the inconvenience.

00:07:02.080 --> 00:07:03.000
Stop it.

00:07:03.080 --> 00:07:08.260
To have one or not,
people should be free to choose.

00:07:08.380 --> 00:07:11.890
People are free to choose
to have one or not

00:07:11.970 --> 00:07:15.760
only if you can pay
attention in class.

00:07:16.390 --> 00:07:18.770
Without your mobile phones

00:07:18.890 --> 00:07:21.600
maybe you feel more anxious
than inconvenienced.

00:07:23.730 --> 00:07:24.900
Saori?

00:07:25.020 --> 00:07:26.780
No! That's not it.

00:07:26.860 --> 00:07:29.860
Then go home after school
and get it.

00:07:29.950 --> 00:07:31.910
That'd be pointless.

00:07:31.990 --> 00:07:34.950
Do you need a mobile phone
during class?

00:07:36.080 --> 00:07:37.740
Not really.

00:07:37.830 --> 00:07:39.450
During recess?

00:07:39.540 --> 00:07:40.160
Yes.

00:07:40.290 --> 00:07:43.120
Why? For an emergency?

00:07:43.290 --> 00:07:46.000
No. For texts and Twitter.

00:07:46.130 --> 00:07:49.420
Must you do them
during recess?

00:07:49.550 --> 00:07:53.550
No... So that's why
I don't use it at school.

00:07:53.760 --> 00:08:00.430
If you don't use it at school,
it means you don't need it at school.

00:08:00.520 --> 00:08:02.310
That's mean.

00:08:02.390 --> 00:08:07.610
People can't concentrate in class
because of their mobiles.

00:08:07.690 --> 00:08:10.860
So maybe you're better off
not bringing them.

00:08:10.990 --> 00:08:15.320
Mistah Sai, you're siding with
the school after all.

00:08:15.490 --> 00:08:17.160
“Mister Saito.”

00:08:17.280 --> 00:08:22.290
When I was your age,
we didn't have mobiles.

00:08:22.620 --> 00:08:25.000
But I won't get into that.

00:08:25.460 --> 00:08:27.380
Real communication

00:08:27.630 --> 00:08:32.470
is more than a mobile
or an Internet connection.

00:08:33.130 --> 00:08:35.550
They're not bad things.

00:08:35.680 --> 00:08:38.720
But in your relationships
with other people

00:08:38.850 --> 00:08:42.520
there are many more important
lessons to be learned.

00:08:42.640 --> 00:08:46.100
That's the consensus,
hence this rule.

00:08:52.150 --> 00:08:57.070
All right. It's finally time to
introduce your new classmate.

00:09:00.370 --> 00:09:02.330
Whoa!

00:09:07.040 --> 00:09:08.380
In time?

00:09:08.460 --> 00:09:09.290
Wrong!

00:09:09.380 --> 00:09:12.670
Seki, the bell rang already.
You're late.

00:09:12.760 --> 00:09:13.720
Oops.

00:09:14.130 --> 00:09:19.180
It's because you wake up early
when you're not a morning person.

00:09:19.260 --> 00:09:20.890
Trying to show off, right?

00:09:21.060 --> 00:09:22.390
Mind your own business.

00:09:22.470 --> 00:09:24.730
Your fly's open again.

00:09:25.690 --> 00:09:27.690
Don't tell anyone, okay?

00:09:27.770 --> 00:09:30.650
You can't boss me around,
Mr. Open Fly.

00:09:31.440 --> 00:09:34.440
Miss Suzuura, will you
please not tell anyone?

00:09:34.570 --> 00:09:36.910
I can't hear you.

00:09:36.990 --> 00:09:39.280
Please don't tell anyone.

00:09:39.530 --> 00:09:40.870
Are you begging me?

00:09:41.370 --> 00:09:42.240
Yes.

00:09:45.540 --> 00:09:47.540
It looks like a fun class.

00:09:47.620 --> 00:09:50.250
This is your new
classmate for real.

00:09:50.340 --> 00:09:51.170
Right?

00:09:51.250 --> 00:09:52.050
Yes.

00:09:52.130 --> 00:09:53.170
Introduce yourself.

00:09:54.050 --> 00:09:57.760
I'm from the city of Hanamaki.

00:09:58.380 --> 00:10:00.640
I don't have my new
uniform yet.

00:10:00.760 --> 00:10:04.100
I'm Ryoichi Kyogoku.
Nice to meet you.

00:10:07.770 --> 00:10:08.730
Hey...

00:10:08.810 --> 00:10:09.480
What?

00:10:09.600 --> 00:10:10.860
It's him.

00:10:16.240 --> 00:10:17.570
You know him?

00:10:17.650 --> 00:10:20.120
I met him this morning.

00:10:20.200 --> 00:10:20.950
This morning?

00:10:36.670 --> 00:10:39.340
Ryoichi, what's your
mobile phone number?

00:10:39.470 --> 00:10:40.340
Number?

00:10:40.470 --> 00:10:41.890
For SMS, you know?

00:10:41.970 --> 00:10:44.470
I don't own a mobile.

00:10:44.560 --> 00:10:46.060
Why not?

00:10:46.140 --> 00:10:47.640
I don't need one.

00:10:48.480 --> 00:10:50.020
Imitating Mistah Sai?

00:10:50.150 --> 00:10:51.980
Strict parents?

00:10:52.110 --> 00:10:56.320
No. I really don't need one.
Is that not a good reason?

00:10:56.400 --> 00:10:57.990
You're kidding.

00:10:58.110 --> 00:11:00.280
You don't even text?

00:11:00.360 --> 00:11:02.030
I don't need to.

00:11:02.160 --> 00:11:07.000
Saori, he really doesn't
have a mobile phone.

00:11:07.080 --> 00:11:09.660
He's not holding
back from you.

00:11:09.790 --> 00:11:10.960
Barn!

00:11:11.290 --> 00:11:12.540
What's up?

00:11:12.670 --> 00:11:14.750
Um... You know...

00:11:15.300 --> 00:11:16.300
Water flea?

00:11:16.380 --> 00:11:19.840
Yeah. Aren't they incredible?

00:11:20.260 --> 00:11:21.930
Hey, wait!

00:11:22.010 --> 00:11:23.010
A play?

00:11:23.140 --> 00:11:25.220
Never been in one, right?

00:11:25.350 --> 00:11:28.850
Mr. Saito is the advisor this year.

00:11:28.930 --> 00:11:32.190
His classes were great last year.

00:11:32.310 --> 00:11:33.060
Really?

00:11:33.190 --> 00:11:35.860
Which club are you
going to join?

00:11:35.940 --> 00:11:38.280
You're tall.
Interested in basketball?

00:11:38.360 --> 00:11:42.030
<i>He looks like he has a secret.</i>

00:11:42.320 --> 00:11:45.160
So what?
I'm sure he does.

00:11:45.240 --> 00:11:46.370
Why do you say that?

00:11:46.450 --> 00:11:47.620
Because he's good-looking.

00:11:47.700 --> 00:11:50.040
So he's your type?

00:11:50.160 --> 00:11:54.500
All the girls were talking about him.

00:11:54.580 --> 00:11:57.090
Like in the locker room.

00:11:57.380 --> 00:11:59.380
You had a dirty thought.

00:11:59.670 --> 00:12:01.340
Ouch!

00:12:01.420 --> 00:12:04.390
Mr. Open Fly...

00:12:04.470 --> 00:12:06.970
Will you drop it?

00:12:07.060 --> 00:12:10.390
Why would a good-looking
guy have a secret?

00:12:10.520 --> 00:12:12.230
That's a girls' secret.

00:12:12.560 --> 00:12:13.390
Huh?

00:12:13.520 --> 00:12:16.860
Open... Mr. Open Fly...

00:12:16.940 --> 00:12:18.400
What's that song?

00:12:19.530 --> 00:12:22.030
Everyone is upset.

00:12:22.110 --> 00:12:23.570
About the mobile phones?

00:12:23.660 --> 00:12:24.410
Yeah.

00:12:24.490 --> 00:12:28.240
My class too. They think
the school's gone too far.

00:12:28.370 --> 00:12:33.500
They're blaming the council for
not organizing an all-school meeting.

00:12:33.620 --> 00:12:35.540
They call us traitors.

00:12:35.630 --> 00:12:39.750
Can I ask each one of you
for your opinion?

00:12:39.840 --> 00:12:41.840
In favor or against it?

00:12:41.920 --> 00:12:43.380
Amano?

00:12:43.470 --> 00:12:46.640
I suppose I'm in favor of it.

00:12:46.760 --> 00:12:48.180
Kondo?

00:12:48.510 --> 00:12:49.760
<i>Favor.</i>

00:12:49.890 --> 00:12:51.220
Kahori?

00:12:51.310 --> 00:12:55.440
Well, they're not an
absolute necessity.

00:12:55.650 --> 00:12:56.310
Jinno?

00:12:56.440 --> 00:12:58.860
Fine then. Favor.

00:12:59.070 --> 00:13:03.570
The girl in that mobile incident
last year was in my class.

00:13:03.650 --> 00:13:07.450
Yuriko Yamagiwa is in
my class this year.

00:13:07.530 --> 00:13:09.530
Mobile phones are convenient.

00:13:09.620 --> 00:13:14.290
But if they hurt someone,
they shouldn't be allowed at school.

00:13:14.410 --> 00:13:16.330
It's only natural.

00:13:17.080 --> 00:13:19.750
You're probably right.

00:13:19.840 --> 00:13:24.090
But people want to be involved
in the decision making.

00:13:24.380 --> 00:13:28.140
It's strange how people
are for it as individuals.

00:13:28.260 --> 00:13:31.010
But as a group,
there's an air of objection.

00:13:31.430 --> 00:13:33.180
Air, huh...

00:13:33.520 --> 00:13:38.520
Are our true feelings
inside our hearts?

00:13:38.770 --> 00:13:41.940
Or are they in the air?

00:13:42.030 --> 00:13:46.860
Obviously, our feelings are
inside ourselves.

00:13:50.030 --> 00:13:52.370
That's not always the case.

00:13:52.490 --> 00:13:55.250
Yes, it is.
What do you mean?

00:13:55.330 --> 00:13:59.540
I think some feelings occur because
of someone other than yourself.

00:13:59.670 --> 00:14:02.750
Are those feelings inside you too?

00:14:02.840 --> 00:14:08.630
Or are they in the air between
people and people?

00:15:17.200 --> 00:15:18.870
Kahori?

00:15:27.550 --> 00:15:29.630
<i>The piano was open.</i>

00:15:30.380 --> 00:15:31.430
<i>Am I not allowed?</i>

00:15:31.510 --> 00:15:33.760
<i>Don't worry. It's okay.</i>

00:15:33.890 --> 00:15:37.140
<i>Anyone can play them
if they're open.</i>

00:15:37.470 --> 00:15:38.810
Okay.

00:15:39.930 --> 00:15:40.810
Thanks.

00:15:41.440 --> 00:15:44.060
Are you going to practice too?

00:15:44.150 --> 00:15:45.820
Yes.

00:15:46.070 --> 00:15:48.150
You're very diligent.

00:15:48.280 --> 00:15:52.110
Not really. I don't have
a piano at home.

00:15:54.910 --> 00:15:55.950
I see.

00:15:58.910 --> 00:16:00.750
“Moonlight”...

00:16:02.580 --> 00:16:04.540
By Debussy, right?

00:16:05.920 --> 00:16:07.000
Yeah.

00:16:20.680 --> 00:16:21.980
I like...

00:16:26.440 --> 00:16:27.690
The moon.

00:16:32.780 --> 00:16:34.030
Is it weird?

00:16:34.160 --> 00:16:37.990
Not at all.
It's not weird at all.

00:16:41.620 --> 00:16:42.210
Okay.

00:16:44.120 --> 00:16:45.120
Good.

00:16:50.170 --> 00:16:51.800
He likes it.

00:16:56.970 --> 00:16:58.550
The moon.

00:17:25.750 --> 00:17:28.920
Sorry to bother you
while you're relaxing.

00:17:29.040 --> 00:17:33.130
You're wasting energy
just by being in this era.

00:17:33.510 --> 00:17:35.590
You are too.

00:17:37.010 --> 00:17:40.510
I'll report your comment
to Doctor Kyogoku.

00:17:40.850 --> 00:17:43.850
I'm sure you haven't
forgotten your mission.

00:17:46.770 --> 00:17:48.600
Moon...

00:17:48.940 --> 00:17:51.940
The moon of this era is yellow.

00:17:52.070 --> 00:17:54.070
It looks odd.

00:17:54.530 --> 00:17:57.150
But beautiful.

00:18:17.300 --> 00:18:19.430
<i>“In tale or history”</i>

00:18:19.510 --> 00:18:23.680
<i>“true love never comes to
a happy end easily.”</i>

00:18:23.760 --> 00:18:26.100
<i>“If people are in love
with each other,”</i>

00:18:26.230 --> 00:18:29.480
<i>“war, death, or sickness”</i>

00:18:29.600 --> 00:18:31.770
<i>“would get in their way.”</i>

00:18:31.900 --> 00:18:34.940
<i>“Then the love melts
away immediately.”</i>

00:18:35.940 --> 00:18:40.160
“Making it momentary as a sound,
swift as a shadow”

00:18:40.450 --> 00:18:42.620
“short as any dream.”

00:18:44.450 --> 00:18:47.460
It's still Lysander's line, right?

00:18:47.540 --> 00:18:50.630
Is there any meaning
in doing plays?

00:18:51.130 --> 00:18:52.040
Meaning?

00:18:52.130 --> 00:18:52.920
Yeah.

00:18:53.000 --> 00:18:56.800
I don't think there's any meaning.

00:18:56.880 --> 00:18:58.050
A necessity?

00:18:58.130 --> 00:19:01.140
No, not a necessity either.

00:19:01.260 --> 00:19:03.100
Then Why?

00:19:04.010 --> 00:19:05.470
So why...

00:19:06.020 --> 00:19:09.480
Kyogoku, you have a
philosophical mind.

00:19:10.480 --> 00:19:11.850
Do you know why?

00:19:11.980 --> 00:19:14.070
You're asking me?

00:19:14.230 --> 00:19:18.780
The man who wrote
“A Midsummer Night's Dream” said

00:19:18.990 --> 00:19:25.200
“acting is holding a mirror up to nature
and showing the form of truth.”

00:19:25.330 --> 00:19:29.580
Mirrors were invented because
people want to see their faces.

00:19:29.660 --> 00:19:33.380
I think acting is the same.

00:19:33.500 --> 00:19:35.250
That's confusing.

00:19:36.670 --> 00:19:42.840
When you act, in the limited time,
momentary you becomes real.

00:19:42.930 --> 00:19:44.760
Momentary?

00:19:44.850 --> 00:19:50.060
Yes. Why don't you look for your
answer in those moments?

00:19:50.310 --> 00:19:53.230
The moments called “now.”

00:19:53.650 --> 00:19:57.480
It sounds like you're
dodging the question.

00:19:57.860 --> 00:20:02.780
I was trying to be cool. I just
want you to enjoy yourselves.

00:20:02.990 --> 00:20:05.410
That's what it means
to be alive.

00:20:05.530 --> 00:20:09.790
Acting is also something
living people do.

00:20:12.540 --> 00:20:14.960
<i>Is Mr. Saito always like that?</i>

00:20:15.040 --> 00:20:19.000
<i>Yeah. Kenji and I were in
his class last year too.</i>

00:20:19.090 --> 00:20:19.920
<i>Oh yeah.</i>

00:20:20.050 --> 00:20:23.380
<i>Mistah Sai is a cool dude
but he hates that name.</i>

00:20:23.470 --> 00:20:25.180
<i>Don't say it to his face.</i>

00:20:25.260 --> 00:20:27.760
<i>It bothers him, huh?</i>

00:20:27.890 --> 00:20:30.140
<i>But it doesn't stop anybody.</i>

00:20:32.390 --> 00:20:35.310
What made you interested in acting?

00:20:35.690 --> 00:20:37.570
Yeah. What?

00:20:39.070 --> 00:20:43.360
I was wondering about the
significance of saying words

00:20:43.450 --> 00:20:45.110
that aren't your real thoughts.

00:20:45.240 --> 00:20:47.240
Wow... Complex.

00:20:47.320 --> 00:20:49.660
What's the purpose
of the process?

00:20:50.040 --> 00:20:51.040
Process?

00:20:51.450 --> 00:20:53.960
I suppose you could
call it that.

00:20:54.080 --> 00:20:59.500
But we're talking now even though
we don't know each other's thoughts.

00:20:59.750 --> 00:21:02.590
In that sense,
it's the same, isn't it?

00:21:02.720 --> 00:21:05.630
Yeah, that's true.

00:21:06.590 --> 00:21:09.510
You're totally lost, aren't you?

00:21:09.600 --> 00:21:10.810
You can tell?

00:21:12.100 --> 00:21:14.690
Sometimes words aren't necessary.

00:21:16.350 --> 00:21:17.100
Yeah.

00:21:17.610 --> 00:21:20.070
I don't get it.
So what?!

00:21:20.150 --> 00:21:24.530
Really? I had a feeling
you understood it all.

00:21:24.950 --> 00:21:26.280
Was I wrong?

00:21:30.370 --> 00:21:32.870
What kind of psychic
power is that?

00:21:41.210 --> 00:21:44.800
Wow! It is an amazing view.

00:21:44.920 --> 00:21:47.550
Isn't it?! Over here.

00:21:48.640 --> 00:21:50.300
A kite?

00:21:50.640 --> 00:21:52.930
I'm not joking.
It's true.

00:21:53.310 --> 00:21:56.850
It stole my lunch
when I was a kid.

00:21:57.650 --> 00:21:59.190
The bad kite.

00:21:59.190 --> 00:22:01.860
Beware of kites

00:21:59.190 --> 00:22:01.860
They steal food

00:22:03.480 --> 00:22:05.990
This place is nice.

00:22:06.110 --> 00:22:07.530
You think so?

00:22:08.490 --> 00:22:10.780
I'm happy to hear that.

00:22:12.450 --> 00:22:15.290
Beware of kites.
They steal food.

00:22:15.500 --> 00:22:16.330
Chomp.

00:22:18.000 --> 00:22:21.710
She'll think you're a
pervert if you keep staring.

00:22:21.840 --> 00:22:23.500
Was I staring?

00:22:23.590 --> 00:22:26.340
Yes. Totally. Gawking.

00:22:26.470 --> 00:22:27.930
What are you doing?

00:22:30.010 --> 00:22:31.890
Nothing.

00:22:43.020 --> 00:22:45.360
You like Kahori that much, huh?

00:22:45.440 --> 00:22:46.780
Are you a psychic?

00:22:46.860 --> 00:22:50.360
Maybe. I can read your mind.

00:22:51.030 --> 00:22:54.410
It was so obvious.
Cheer up.

00:22:54.540 --> 00:22:55.200
I can't.

00:22:55.290 --> 00:22:56.290
Try.

00:22:56.370 --> 00:22:57.540
But...

00:22:59.370 --> 00:23:02.460
You wouldn't understand my feelings.

00:23:06.210 --> 00:23:07.970
Why do you say that?

00:23:08.050 --> 00:23:08.840
Huh?

00:23:08.920 --> 00:23:10.930
How do you know?!

00:23:11.140 --> 00:23:12.390
Natsuki?

00:23:31.070 --> 00:23:32.240
Natsuki!

00:23:42.330 --> 00:23:45.840
<i>This is the symbol
you drew, is it not?</i>

00:23:46.210 --> 00:23:49.720
<i>Yes! I can't believe it!</i>

00:23:49.800 --> 00:23:52.180
<i>I read your mind.</i>

00:23:52.380 --> 00:23:53.640
<i>Wow!</i>

00:23:55.260 --> 00:23:57.810
<i>Telepathy, law of physics.</i>

00:24:00.020 --> 00:24:02.350
People can't read
people's minds.

00:24:02.560 --> 00:24:05.230
That's true.

00:24:05.310 --> 00:24:09.280
Being psychic would be
convenient but I'm not.

00:24:10.030 --> 00:24:12.360
It's like owning
a mobile phone.

00:24:12.450 --> 00:24:15.740
At my age, it makes no difference
if I have one or not.

00:24:15.820 --> 00:24:17.620
It's about your age?

00:24:17.700 --> 00:24:22.790
I have one only because others
find it inconvenient if I don't.

00:24:23.120 --> 00:24:25.290
Are you a psychic?

00:24:25.710 --> 00:24:28.710
I'm talking about mobile phones.

00:24:28.920 --> 00:24:31.880
Why do you want
to be a psychic?

00:24:34.890 --> 00:24:38.760
Have you ever wanted to know
someone's feelings?

00:24:38.850 --> 00:24:40.560
Their real feelings.

00:24:43.230 --> 00:24:45.810
You're so perceptive.

00:24:45.940 --> 00:24:48.440
Thanks for cheering me up.

00:24:49.730 --> 00:24:52.740
Kenji, go help your dad
in the kitchen!

00:24:52.820 --> 00:24:54.200
Okay!

00:25:51.800 --> 00:25:53.800
Hey, that's enough!

00:25:56.010 --> 00:25:57.180
You okay?

00:25:57.260 --> 00:25:58.890
Sorry! Sorry!

00:25:59.140 --> 00:26:00.890
What do you want?

00:26:01.140 --> 00:26:03.220
You won't answer
your mobile.

00:26:03.350 --> 00:26:04.390
Because...

00:26:04.520 --> 00:26:07.190
I wanted to apologize
for earlier.

00:26:08.400 --> 00:26:12.070
I'm sorry for saying you wouldn't
understand my feelings.

00:26:12.190 --> 00:26:13.780
I'll tell you how I feel.

00:26:13.900 --> 00:26:16.990
You see... I...

00:26:18.570 --> 00:26:20.070
I've had...

00:26:22.160 --> 00:26:24.700
A crush on Kahori
for a while now.

00:26:25.830 --> 00:26:29.580
So I wanted to talk
to you about her.

00:26:29.750 --> 00:26:31.460
You're a jerk!

00:26:38.050 --> 00:26:39.260
Why?

00:27:32.400 --> 00:27:33.610
You can't do it.

00:27:52.250 --> 00:27:53.670
Why?

00:27:54.330 --> 00:27:56.340
Why did you help me?

00:27:56.590 --> 00:28:03.090
Because you didn't intend
to jump in the first place.

00:28:08.770 --> 00:28:11.350
What do you mean?
Who are you?!

00:28:12.350 --> 00:28:17.940
You're Yuriko Yamagiwa,
2nd year in middle school, again.

00:28:18.150 --> 00:28:21.650
You think nobody understands
your feelings

00:28:21.820 --> 00:28:26.120
so you were going to jump
but in truth, you don't want to die.

00:28:26.200 --> 00:28:29.700
Shut up!
You don't even know me!

00:28:30.290 --> 00:28:34.630
Know you?
I don't need to.

00:28:37.290 --> 00:28:41.380
I understand.
I can hear it.

00:28:41.800 --> 00:28:44.050
The voice in your heart.

00:28:52.020 --> 00:28:54.810
You want to live
more than anybody.

00:28:56.400 --> 00:28:58.900
It's tough not being understood.

00:28:59.020 --> 00:29:01.030
Stop it!

00:29:06.240 --> 00:29:07.240
Ryoichi...

00:29:07.370 --> 00:29:09.620
I know.

00:29:09.740 --> 00:29:11.910
She's perfect.

00:29:20.420 --> 00:29:24.050
You want to read people's
minds, don't you?

00:29:24.590 --> 00:29:26.260
Wait... What...

00:29:26.390 --> 00:29:28.300
You have the power.

00:29:28.430 --> 00:29:32.600
Without it, your voice wouldn't
be reaching me.

00:29:32.930 --> 00:29:35.940
I don't get it! Stop!

00:29:37.900 --> 00:29:39.690
Come here.

00:29:39.940 --> 00:29:45.110
Come here and nobody
can lie to you anymore.

00:30:14.310 --> 00:30:16.060
<i>Hello? Kaho?</i>

00:30:16.940 --> 00:30:18.690
Oh, sorry.

00:30:19.310 --> 00:30:22.320
I'll wait and eat with you.

00:30:24.150 --> 00:30:26.650
I'll see you when
you finish work.

00:30:27.320 --> 00:30:28.450
Bye.

00:30:54.680 --> 00:30:58.190
Natsu... Hey, Natsu!

00:30:58.770 --> 00:31:02.610
What is it?
I'm sleepy.

00:31:02.690 --> 00:31:06.820
I get sleepy when I'm angry.
You have a problem with that?

00:31:07.110 --> 00:31:10.860
They're really pretty.
Can you see?

00:31:11.030 --> 00:31:13.330
Natsu, look!

00:31:13.450 --> 00:31:18.210
Will you stop bothering me?
What is it?

00:31:18.330 --> 00:31:22.420
Natsu, aren't they so cool?!

00:31:22.540 --> 00:31:28.510
I like you.
I like you so much, Kenji.

00:31:33.300 --> 00:31:35.510
Aren't they cool?!

00:31:36.140 --> 00:31:39.810
We can see better over there.

00:31:43.230 --> 00:31:45.900
So tell me...

00:31:47.360 --> 00:31:50.900
What are you gonna be
when you grow up?

00:31:51.990 --> 00:31:56.870
I'm gonna run the inn
because everyone loves it.

00:31:57.740 --> 00:31:59.250
Good.

00:32:00.080 --> 00:32:03.830
So you'll always be my
next-door neighbor.

00:32:05.000 --> 00:32:08.090
You won't go to Tokyo
or something?

00:32:08.380 --> 00:32:11.550
I like you so much...

00:32:11.630 --> 00:32:12.630
What?

00:32:13.510 --> 00:32:15.760
I really, really like you.

00:32:15.890 --> 00:32:16.600
Huh?

00:32:18.270 --> 00:32:19.930
I like you, Kenji.

00:32:20.270 --> 00:32:21.730
So much!

00:32:22.480 --> 00:32:23.440
What?

00:32:23.940 --> 00:32:26.940
I like you.
I like you so much.

00:32:27.070 --> 00:32:28.110
So much!

00:32:37.870 --> 00:32:38.740
I'm saying...!

00:32:40.910 --> 00:32:44.000
I like you so much, Kenji.

00:32:44.120 --> 00:32:47.170
I like you so, so much!

00:33:01.100 --> 00:33:02.770
<i>I had a dream.</i>

00:33:04.640 --> 00:33:08.480
<i>The dream I hadn't
had in a while.</i>

00:33:10.980 --> 00:33:12.490
Natsuki!

00:33:13.070 --> 00:33:14.530
Are you awake?

00:33:15.160 --> 00:33:16.320
<i>I realize now</i>

00:33:16.780 --> 00:33:21.790
<i>that day, our hands were connected
but our hearts weren't.</i>

00:33:22.950 --> 00:33:26.630
<i>We've lived next door to
each other all our lives.</i>

00:33:26.710 --> 00:33:32.210
<i>Same pre-school, same grade
school, same middle school...</i>

00:33:32.420 --> 00:33:34.300
<i>Same homeroom.</i>

00:33:34.510 --> 00:33:38.090
<i>Our student IDs and lockers
are next to each other.</i>

00:33:39.010 --> 00:33:41.100
<i>Forever the girl next door.</i>

00:33:41.180 --> 00:33:44.640
<i>Yes, that's me.</i>

00:33:44.850 --> 00:33:49.810
<i>Always was, still am,
and will be from now on.</i>

00:33:49.980 --> 00:33:54.070
<i>Forever and ever.</i>

00:33:56.360 --> 00:33:57.110
Natsuki!

00:34:09.380 --> 00:34:11.380
<i>I Wish...</i>

00:34:14.210 --> 00:34:16.840
<i>I could stop liking him.</i>

00:34:36.400 --> 00:34:38.410
Go on in.

00:34:38.740 --> 00:34:40.950
Excuse me... Passing through.

00:34:41.910 --> 00:34:43.700
Good morning, Yuriko.

00:34:43.790 --> 00:34:45.580
Good morning, Natsuki.

00:34:45.660 --> 00:34:48.540
You know my name?

00:34:48.620 --> 00:34:50.250
From the seating chart.

00:34:50.540 --> 00:34:51.710
Good morning.

00:34:52.380 --> 00:34:53.710
Good morning.

00:35:01.760 --> 00:35:05.470
<i>Yuriko looked so calm and confident.</i>

00:35:05.600 --> 00:35:09.940
Yeah. I wonder why she decided
to start coming to school now.

00:35:10.020 --> 00:35:11.770
I'm glad she did though.

00:35:11.900 --> 00:35:13.320
You were worried about her?

00:35:13.440 --> 00:35:17.610
Sort of... Because I've never
been absent from school.

00:35:17.690 --> 00:35:20.360
You still have a
perfect attendance?

00:35:20.450 --> 00:35:21.450
Yep.

00:35:21.570 --> 00:35:24.740
Miss Suzuura, any concerns
about your record?

00:35:24.830 --> 00:35:26.160
Sickness, no.

00:35:26.290 --> 00:35:28.290
How about a love sickness?

00:35:29.540 --> 00:35:30.710
No way.

00:35:30.790 --> 00:35:33.460
You never know.
You might fall in love.

00:35:33.590 --> 00:35:39.840
Impossible. But if I did fall in love,
I'd come to school to see him.

00:35:39.970 --> 00:35:42.050
Yeah, that's true.

00:35:42.140 --> 00:35:44.800
I know... The new
guy is hot, isn't he?

00:35:47.220 --> 00:35:51.730
You're going to tell
me everything today.

00:36:35.650 --> 00:36:38.570
You're here already, Kenji.

00:36:42.200 --> 00:36:43.490
What are you doing here?

00:36:45.160 --> 00:36:49.740
You're not making any sense.
How should I respond to that?

00:36:49.870 --> 00:36:52.660
Oh... I just thought...

00:36:53.500 --> 00:36:55.420
Sorry. My mistake.

00:36:55.580 --> 00:36:57.920
Sorry about that.

00:37:03.550 --> 00:37:05.180
Shots of the sky?

00:37:05.590 --> 00:37:06.720
No. Clouds.

00:37:06.800 --> 00:37:07.800
Clouds?

00:37:08.510 --> 00:37:10.770
Clouds that look like something.

00:37:10.890 --> 00:37:13.730
What does this look like?

00:37:14.390 --> 00:37:16.860
This? A hamburger.

00:37:16.940 --> 00:37:19.070
Oh... How about this?

00:37:19.150 --> 00:37:20.320
A cheeseburger.

00:37:20.400 --> 00:37:21.860
That's funny!

00:37:22.780 --> 00:37:27.660
Look closely. This part looks
like melted cheese...

00:37:29.910 --> 00:37:32.250
Hungry, huh?

00:37:43.840 --> 00:37:46.430
So love at first sight
really happens.

00:37:46.760 --> 00:37:51.430
I'm sorry. I feel like I unloaded
everything on you.

00:37:51.640 --> 00:37:54.270
You have to vent your
feelings sometimes.

00:37:54.350 --> 00:37:56.690
You're too much
of a good girl.

00:37:57.270 --> 00:37:59.940
I'm not a good girl at all.

00:38:00.270 --> 00:38:04.860
Oh, come on...
The new guy is so lucky.

00:38:05.950 --> 00:38:08.360
He plays the piano
really well too.

00:38:12.790 --> 00:38:17.040
It's so strange that I feel this way.

00:38:17.120 --> 00:38:18.120
No, it's not.

00:38:18.250 --> 00:38:23.630
Sometimes you can't explain why
you like someone so much.

00:38:23.760 --> 00:38:24.960
You think so?

00:38:25.090 --> 00:38:28.640
Yes. I really think so.

00:38:32.470 --> 00:38:35.640
So when are you going to
tell him how you feel?

00:38:35.730 --> 00:38:38.230
I'm not going to.

00:38:38.310 --> 00:38:43.820
Why not? Before we know it,
we'll be graduating middle school.

00:38:44.480 --> 00:38:47.030
That's fine with me.

00:38:55.660 --> 00:39:00.000
Wow! Was the view from here
always this pretty?

00:39:01.670 --> 00:39:07.010
I think this is the most beautiful
sunset I've ever seen.

00:39:10.760 --> 00:39:11.760
So...

00:39:12.010 --> 00:39:13.180
Yeah?

00:39:13.510 --> 00:39:16.270
Aren't you attracted to anybody?

00:39:16.350 --> 00:39:18.140
No. Nobody.

00:39:18.230 --> 00:39:20.600
I don't believe you.
How about Kenji?

00:39:20.770 --> 00:39:25.020
Oh, please. Just because
we're next-door neighbors...

00:39:26.030 --> 00:39:29.490
He's an insensitive jerk.

00:39:30.360 --> 00:39:34.120
Oh... So he's really not the one?

00:39:39.330 --> 00:39:39.910
Natsuki?

00:39:40.040 --> 00:39:43.710
He and I are next-door neighbors.

00:39:43.880 --> 00:39:47.590
Nothing more, nothing less.

00:39:47.710 --> 00:39:52.550
Ask him. I'm sure he'll
say the same thing.

00:39:57.390 --> 00:39:59.980
You're kind of weird, Kyogoku.

00:40:00.600 --> 00:40:01.770
Why?

00:40:01.900 --> 00:40:04.480
You've never eaten
a hamburger.

00:40:04.560 --> 00:40:06.690
That makes me weird?

00:40:06.770 --> 00:40:09.740
Yes. Are your parents strict?

00:40:10.780 --> 00:40:13.410
No. Nothing like that.

00:40:14.740 --> 00:40:16.120
Incredible.

00:40:21.750 --> 00:40:25.420
There's something
I want to ask you.

00:40:25.710 --> 00:40:26.790
What is it?

00:40:26.920 --> 00:40:31.010
When we first met, did you
say, "So this is Earth."?

00:40:31.420 --> 00:40:33.340
Did you say that
to anyone?

00:40:33.430 --> 00:40:34.930
No. Why?

00:40:35.050 --> 00:40:36.640
They'll think I'm weird.

00:40:36.760 --> 00:40:38.600
They already do.

00:40:39.770 --> 00:40:42.190
You were wearing headphones.

00:40:44.100 --> 00:40:45.270
Yeah, I was.

00:40:45.400 --> 00:40:47.770
If you heard me,
you're a psychic.

00:40:47.860 --> 00:40:49.030
True.

00:40:49.400 --> 00:40:50.610
I said it.

00:40:52.280 --> 00:40:55.110
I said it in my mind.

00:40:55.240 --> 00:40:58.240
I think you're a psychic.

00:40:59.740 --> 00:41:01.580
Are you serious?

00:41:01.660 --> 00:41:03.290
Of course.

00:41:03.370 --> 00:41:05.120
Then are you an alien?

00:41:05.250 --> 00:41:08.670
I'm more like a guy
from the future.

00:41:10.460 --> 00:41:13.220
So a psychic
and a guy from the future

00:41:13.300 --> 00:41:17.010
are eating hamburgers
in the sunset.

00:41:17.800 --> 00:41:19.140
That's right.

00:41:21.640 --> 00:41:24.520
That's exactly right.

00:41:29.320 --> 00:41:33.320
<i>I'll bring from the future
the food you're craving.</i>

00:41:33.440 --> 00:41:37.450
<i>Three, two, one, open.</i>

00:41:37.530 --> 00:41:39.120
From the future...

00:41:41.410 --> 00:41:44.460
<i>Time warp, law of physics.</i>

00:41:46.000 --> 00:41:50.130
Ryoichi, you ate food from this era.

00:41:50.800 --> 00:41:53.130
Don't get involved more
than you have to.

00:41:53.210 --> 00:41:56.010
The kid, Kenji, you know he's...

00:41:56.090 --> 00:41:58.850
An obstacle in our plan.

00:41:59.470 --> 00:42:02.890
Dad chose this era
because he's here.

00:42:03.520 --> 00:42:04.810
To get revenge.

00:42:05.640 --> 00:42:09.900
I'm not authorized to
speak on his behalf.

00:42:10.060 --> 00:42:12.230
Will there be a battle?

00:42:12.440 --> 00:42:17.110
He's a dangerous wild card.
That's all I can say.

00:42:17.860 --> 00:42:20.370
Let's continue the program.

00:42:20.490 --> 00:42:22.990
We have several
power-user candidates.

00:42:23.700 --> 00:42:28.880
People of this era should
handle their own affairs.

00:42:50.560 --> 00:42:52.570
<i>You're running a lot lately.</i>

00:42:52.650 --> 00:42:57.700
I want to go to high school in Tokyo
and join the track team.

00:42:57.780 --> 00:42:59.950
Wow! A sports nomination.

00:43:00.070 --> 00:43:03.950
I just started thinking about it.

00:43:04.080 --> 00:43:05.830
Team practice after school?

00:43:05.910 --> 00:43:07.080
Yeah.

00:43:07.540 --> 00:43:09.040
And you?
The council?

00:43:09.120 --> 00:43:11.750
A meeting about
the mobile phones.

00:43:11.830 --> 00:43:15.340
Something about punishing
students who break the rule.

00:43:15.550 --> 00:43:18.260
Then piano practice, right?
Maybe I'll see you.

00:43:18.380 --> 00:43:20.720
Really? I'll wait for you.

00:43:24.560 --> 00:43:27.270
They're together a lot
these days.

00:43:27.430 --> 00:43:28.100
You think?

00:43:28.230 --> 00:43:31.650
Oops... Not that it
means anything.

00:43:32.150 --> 00:43:33.560
It doesn't bother me.

00:43:33.650 --> 00:43:34.610
Come on...

00:43:34.690 --> 00:43:37.110
No talking about this at school.

00:43:37.400 --> 00:43:38.820
What part of speech is this?

00:43:38.950 --> 00:43:40.700
Japanese!

00:43:40.780 --> 00:43:41.780
Um...

00:43:42.070 --> 00:43:43.660
Japanese.

00:43:43.780 --> 00:43:44.580
A prefix.

00:43:44.780 --> 00:43:48.290
Yes, a prefix.
What comes after this?

00:43:48.450 --> 00:43:49.080
Japanese.

00:43:49.160 --> 00:43:50.160
Toyama!

00:43:50.290 --> 00:43:51.620
You still mad?

00:43:52.630 --> 00:43:54.790
I'm sorry about the acorns.

00:43:55.290 --> 00:43:58.300
Come on. I'm sorry.

00:43:58.800 --> 00:44:00.010
Did it hurt that much?

00:44:03.800 --> 00:44:05.300
Yes.

00:44:06.310 --> 00:44:08.060
My heart ached.

00:44:08.390 --> 00:44:10.560
Huh? Heart?

00:44:10.980 --> 00:44:12.560
As in chest...

00:44:15.900 --> 00:44:17.820
No... No...

00:44:18.650 --> 00:44:20.280
You're awful!

00:44:22.740 --> 00:44:23.950
Jerk!

00:44:25.450 --> 00:44:26.620
Natsuki!

00:44:26.700 --> 00:44:30.580
Ouch!!!

00:44:35.840 --> 00:44:39.010
Oh... Kaho's not here yet.

00:45:01.860 --> 00:45:04.280
Did you see Soga?

00:45:04.360 --> 00:45:07.490
President Soga?
I didn't see her.

00:45:07.660 --> 00:45:08.870
She's absent today.

00:45:08.990 --> 00:45:11.950
But I saw her this morning.

00:45:12.370 --> 00:45:14.040
Really?

00:45:14.170 --> 00:45:18.340
She wasn't at the meeting.
Maybe she left early.

00:45:50.160 --> 00:45:52.830
What's going on?

00:45:52.910 --> 00:45:57.880
A ritual to become a human
who can live in the future.

00:45:57.960 --> 00:45:59.750
Haruka Soga passed the test.

00:46:00.090 --> 00:46:01.750
What?

00:46:01.840 --> 00:46:04.380
But you don't. I'm sorry.

00:46:05.090 --> 00:46:08.890
I can't hear the voice in your heart.

00:46:09.430 --> 00:46:12.430
You should keep your mouth shut.

00:46:12.560 --> 00:46:15.980
Are you trying to increase
my work load?

00:46:16.100 --> 00:46:18.350
What?! It talked!

00:46:18.440 --> 00:46:21.610
I wish you were like us.

00:46:21.900 --> 00:46:25.700
Too bad because you're
a really nice person.

00:46:26.900 --> 00:46:28.070
Ouch!

00:46:29.030 --> 00:46:31.200
This hurts!

00:46:39.830 --> 00:46:42.340
Help! Kenji, help!

00:46:42.460 --> 00:46:43.550
Stop it.

00:46:49.510 --> 00:46:51.260
That hurt!

00:46:53.140 --> 00:46:54.220
Ryoichi?

00:46:56.060 --> 00:46:57.390
Are you okay?

00:46:59.650 --> 00:47:02.820
Don't tell anyone
about today, okay?

00:47:02.900 --> 00:47:06.400
Who are you?
What are you?

00:47:06.490 --> 00:47:08.150
Human beings. No?

00:47:08.280 --> 00:47:10.780
You look like human beings but...

00:47:10.870 --> 00:47:15.040
People are coming.
We better go.

00:47:19.000 --> 00:47:23.670
Not too bad that the student
council president has the power.

00:47:23.750 --> 00:47:26.340
We can accelerate the plan.

00:47:50.200 --> 00:47:51.740
Kahori...

00:47:53.200 --> 00:47:54.580
I'm glad you're here.

00:47:56.540 --> 00:48:00.120
I borrowed this without asking.
Thanks.

00:48:01.540 --> 00:48:04.880
Are you going to practice
“Moonlight” too?

00:48:05.000 --> 00:48:09.130
Yes... I want to learn
how to play it.

00:48:10.550 --> 00:48:13.390
I want to hear you
play it one day.

00:48:20.230 --> 00:48:22.690
What's taking Natsuki so long?

00:48:42.920 --> 00:48:46.420
<i>I don't remember my father.</i>

00:48:47.000 --> 00:48:48.920
<i>He was a fisherman.</i>

00:48:49.090 --> 00:48:50.260
<i>One stormy night</i>

00:48:50.710 --> 00:48:56.140
<i>he drowned trying to save
his friend who fell off a boat.</i>

00:48:57.430 --> 00:49:01.350
<i>My mother is afraid of the sea.</i>

00:49:01.770 --> 00:49:04.770
<i>She worries about me
being here.</i>

00:49:04.850 --> 00:49:11.360
<i>Coming to the sea is my
only act of rebellion.</i>

00:49:13.610 --> 00:49:18.370
<i>Because I think Dad
wasn't afraid of the sea.</i>

00:49:20.120 --> 00:49:24.620
<i>This is the only place where
I can feel my father.</i>

00:49:25.370 --> 00:49:28.380
<i>Where I can talk to him.</i>

00:49:38.550 --> 00:49:39.640
Shiro!

00:49:39.760 --> 00:49:41.310
Sorry, Kahori!

00:49:41.970 --> 00:49:45.480
Good boy.
How old is he?

00:49:45.560 --> 00:49:48.440
Pretty old.
In his teens.

00:49:48.520 --> 00:49:50.480
He's that old?

00:49:50.570 --> 00:49:53.740
We've had him since
I was a small kid.

00:49:53.820 --> 00:49:55.530
He looks younger.

00:49:55.650 --> 00:49:57.950
Yeah? I wonder why.

00:50:00.660 --> 00:50:02.330
By the way...

00:50:02.830 --> 00:50:04.000
Did you see Natsuki today?

00:50:04.250 --> 00:50:07.500
No. She hasn't come
to school for days.

00:50:09.040 --> 00:50:10.170
Have you talked to her?

00:50:10.250 --> 00:50:12.300
No. She won't
answer her phone.

00:50:13.340 --> 00:50:15.840
She doesn't take
my calls either.

00:50:15.930 --> 00:50:17.590
I'm worried.

00:50:20.010 --> 00:50:22.350
Her perfect attendance
record stopped.

00:50:22.430 --> 00:50:23.970
You knew about it?

00:50:24.060 --> 00:50:26.690
She told me.

00:50:26.940 --> 00:50:28.690
Now it's just me.

00:50:28.810 --> 00:50:30.310
You too?

00:50:30.400 --> 00:50:31.820
I'm always late though.

00:50:38.700 --> 00:50:40.030
Um...!

00:50:40.120 --> 00:50:40.700
Yes?

00:50:40.820 --> 00:50:45.370
Are you interested in
anyone right now?

00:51:07.060 --> 00:51:12.730
Students are forbidden to bring
mobiles to school.

00:51:13.070 --> 00:51:18.740
But many are breaking the rule
and secretly bringing them.

00:51:18.900 --> 00:51:22.070
They should be punished strictly.

00:51:22.280 --> 00:51:24.620
We should make a proposal...

00:51:25.080 --> 00:51:27.830
Suspended? That strict?

00:51:28.750 --> 00:51:30.920
For disobeying the school rule.

00:51:31.000 --> 00:51:36.670
I know that! But do we even have
the authority to decide?!

00:51:36.760 --> 00:51:38.550
We do have the authority.

00:51:38.760 --> 00:51:41.430
Supplement 2 of Article 10.

00:51:41.510 --> 00:51:45.850
“The student council may propose
rules when deemed necessary.”

00:51:46.770 --> 00:51:49.890
The rules become effective upon
the student assembly's approval.

00:51:50.770 --> 00:51:52.770
Yeah but...

00:51:52.860 --> 00:51:58.190
It also says “in case of an emergency,
they become effective immediately.”

00:51:58.280 --> 00:52:00.450
The advisor has to approve.

00:52:00.570 --> 00:52:03.870
Mr. Yamada is on sick leave
starting today.

00:52:04.490 --> 00:52:06.990
Then advisor approval
won't be necessary.

00:52:07.120 --> 00:52:10.460
Wait! He was fine yesterday...

00:52:10.540 --> 00:52:13.130
Yeah. What happened?

00:52:14.630 --> 00:52:16.960
Let's take a vote.

00:52:17.050 --> 00:52:18.760
We haven't discussed...

00:52:18.840 --> 00:52:20.510
Those in favor?

00:52:22.470 --> 00:52:25.800
See? This is crazy...

00:52:28.350 --> 00:52:28.970
Why?

00:52:29.060 --> 00:52:31.230
We have the majority.

00:52:34.060 --> 00:52:35.480
Yukari...

00:52:38.570 --> 00:52:41.950
This rule has been approved
by the council.

00:52:46.080 --> 00:52:47.740
What's going on?

00:52:47.830 --> 00:52:48.830
I don't know.

00:52:48.950 --> 00:52:52.870
Everybody seems like
a different person.

00:52:53.000 --> 00:52:55.420
I said I don't know!

00:52:57.670 --> 00:52:58.460
Sorry.

00:52:59.670 --> 00:53:01.840
Haven't you felt it?

00:53:01.920 --> 00:53:06.010
Strange things are
happening around me.

00:53:07.010 --> 00:53:10.100
People's personalities
are suddenly changing.

00:53:10.180 --> 00:53:13.270
One student after another.

00:53:14.560 --> 00:53:18.570
On the other hand, many have
stopped coming to school.

00:53:18.690 --> 00:53:21.940
23 in total.

00:53:22.030 --> 00:53:23.360
So many?

00:53:23.490 --> 00:53:25.410
I'm worried too.

00:53:25.530 --> 00:53:29.200
None of them are
responding to my calls.

00:53:29.280 --> 00:53:33.460
People are anxious and that's why
they bring their mobiles.

00:53:33.960 --> 00:53:35.960
They feel lonely at school.

00:53:36.880 --> 00:53:42.420
But the ones who have changed
act like nothings wrong. To me...

00:53:44.220 --> 00:53:48.390
You might think I've gone crazy too.

00:53:48.470 --> 00:53:50.560
What? Tell me.

00:53:52.730 --> 00:53:55.890
It's like they're communicating
without words.

00:53:58.900 --> 00:54:03.070
Like telepathy.
Does it seem like that to you?

00:54:06.320 --> 00:54:11.580
Do you want to visit Mr. Yamada
after school?

00:54:11.740 --> 00:54:14.370
Yeah. I'm worried
about him too.

00:54:14.830 --> 00:54:17.000
Let me go home first.

00:54:17.420 --> 00:54:19.420
Let's get in touch
on our mobiles.

00:54:19.500 --> 00:54:24.090
Um... I don't have a mobile phone.

00:54:32.720 --> 00:54:36.190
Natsuki's not even
answering her phone.

00:54:36.270 --> 00:54:38.020
Doesn't she want
her pillow?

00:54:39.270 --> 00:54:40.940
Waiting for someone?

00:54:41.610 --> 00:54:42.780
Yes.

00:54:42.860 --> 00:54:46.200
Do you mind if I waited with you?

00:54:46.450 --> 00:54:48.240
No, I don't mind.

00:54:49.200 --> 00:54:52.120
Really? Good.

00:54:56.290 --> 00:55:00.630
I wanted mobile phones to
disappear from the world.

00:55:01.540 --> 00:55:06.880
They're nothing but trouble.
They can harm you and others.

00:55:06.970 --> 00:55:09.470
Such a flawed tool.

00:55:09.640 --> 00:55:11.550
Flawed?

00:55:11.890 --> 00:55:16.810
You're not alone...
You're always connected to others...

00:55:16.930 --> 00:55:23.770
A silly device that people use to lie
to themselves and avoid reality.

00:55:25.650 --> 00:55:30.820
Why use mobile phones?
In this world, there's a perfect way.

00:55:38.580 --> 00:55:42.580
I wanted to warn you.

00:55:42.670 --> 00:55:43.670
Warn me?

00:55:43.790 --> 00:55:50.010
What you're trying to do
won't be good for anybody.

00:55:50.680 --> 00:55:53.850
Jinno, vice president
of the student council...

00:55:54.100 --> 00:55:57.100
Too bad he missed his date.

00:55:57.720 --> 00:55:58.890
What happened?

00:55:59.690 --> 00:56:00.690
He moved.

00:56:02.020 --> 00:56:04.940
People are better off
without mobile phones.

00:56:05.020 --> 00:56:08.780
That way, they wish for
the power we have.

00:56:09.440 --> 00:56:15.780
Now aren't you curious about
people's true thoughts?

00:56:17.540 --> 00:56:22.290
It's lonely when you don't
know people's real feelings.

00:56:22.370 --> 00:56:25.880
When people don't
understand yours.

00:56:26.210 --> 00:56:29.970
But... What can you do about it?

00:56:30.300 --> 00:56:32.050
Be born again.

00:56:32.380 --> 00:56:37.390
In the future, people can't
live without that power.

00:56:37.890 --> 00:56:40.310
That's what he said
so it must be true.

00:56:40.390 --> 00:56:43.560
He? Are you talking about...

00:56:46.650 --> 00:56:48.480
Do you want to try?

00:56:49.400 --> 00:56:50.820
Why don't you?

00:56:52.400 --> 00:56:54.990
Try? Try what?

00:56:55.070 --> 00:56:56.740
It's like soap bubbles.

00:56:56.870 --> 00:56:58.540
Soap bubbles?

00:56:59.580 --> 00:57:03.500
Everybody has her own
world inside her.

00:57:05.040 --> 00:57:09.800
Look at the worlds inside
the soap bubbles.

00:57:10.090 --> 00:57:13.930
But the worlds aren't connected.

00:57:14.090 --> 00:57:15.930
It's lonely.

00:57:16.260 --> 00:57:19.770
So we'll connect them.

00:57:20.350 --> 00:57:22.600
See? Not lonely anymore.

00:57:24.690 --> 00:57:25.600
They'll disappear.

00:57:25.730 --> 00:57:27.060
Normally yes.

00:57:27.150 --> 00:57:31.150
That's why you have to try
and see if you have the power.

00:57:57.140 --> 00:57:58.260
Kahori!

00:58:07.730 --> 00:58:09.560
What happened?!

00:58:10.650 --> 00:58:12.480
Are you okay?!

00:58:14.150 --> 00:58:15.530
<i>Are you okay?</i>

00:58:17.160 --> 00:58:18.740
Let's get out of here.

00:58:19.070 --> 00:58:22.830
Hold on. I'm fine.
I can stand up.

00:58:23.160 --> 00:58:24.000
Sorry.

00:58:24.080 --> 00:58:25.580
It's okay.

00:58:25.660 --> 00:58:27.120
Wait!

00:58:34.840 --> 00:58:38.840
Are you sure he was
born with the power?

00:58:39.340 --> 00:58:41.850
He didn't respond to my voice.

00:58:41.930 --> 00:58:44.680
But he came to help her.

00:58:44.810 --> 00:58:45.980
And that power...

00:58:46.060 --> 00:58:48.020
Maybe Kahori has the power.

00:58:48.100 --> 00:58:50.650
No, not her.

00:58:51.020 --> 00:58:54.030
The boy's power has been blocked.

00:58:54.280 --> 00:58:58.780
And I have an idea
who did it and why.

00:58:58.860 --> 00:59:01.700
Sorry. I was still
holding your hand.

00:59:08.210 --> 00:59:09.370
Hi there.

00:59:09.460 --> 00:59:10.960
Grandpa!

00:59:11.040 --> 00:59:14.000
My room is upstairs.

00:59:14.090 --> 00:59:16.510
Let's talk there,
if you don't mind.

00:59:17.420 --> 00:59:19.550
I'll get something to drink.

00:59:21.220 --> 00:59:23.970
Iced tea... Iced tea...

01:00:03.260 --> 01:00:05.260
No... This isn't...

01:00:05.350 --> 01:00:07.600
I'm sorry to intrude.

01:00:07.720 --> 01:00:10.890
Hey, please!

01:00:12.020 --> 01:00:14.520
I was so surprised.

01:00:16.190 --> 01:00:17.610
Me too.

01:00:17.730 --> 01:00:21.660
Natsuki, stop sneaking into
my room from the window.

01:00:21.780 --> 01:00:24.620
Then stop shooting acorns.

01:00:24.700 --> 01:00:27.290
You fell once and
broke your leg.

01:00:27.410 --> 01:00:29.080
That was you.

01:00:29.160 --> 01:00:30.460
It was?

01:00:30.540 --> 01:00:34.040
When we were talking on
the paper-cup phones...

01:00:37.550 --> 01:00:41.550
Being here makes what happened
earlier seem like a dream.

01:00:41.630 --> 01:00:43.970
Did it really happen?

01:00:44.090 --> 01:00:46.180
Do you feel okay?

01:00:46.300 --> 01:00:48.430
Thanks. I'm not afraid anymore.

01:00:48.970 --> 01:00:53.230
Afraid? Did the new guy
threaten you too?

01:00:59.320 --> 01:01:01.990
Did Kyogoku do something to you?

01:01:02.070 --> 01:01:02.740
Forget it.

01:01:02.820 --> 01:01:05.950
Is that why you stopped
coming to school?

01:01:06.030 --> 01:01:07.200
I don't know anything.

01:01:07.330 --> 01:01:08.660
I thought so.

01:01:09.540 --> 01:01:14.540
He has something to do with
what's happening at school.

01:01:16.750 --> 01:01:22.920
Natsuki, I want to know what he's
trying to do at our school.

01:01:24.720 --> 01:01:26.430
Tell me, Natsuki.

01:01:27.010 --> 01:01:28.600
What happened?

01:01:50.700 --> 01:01:52.040
<i>I see.</i>

01:01:52.370 --> 01:01:54.620
That means...

01:01:57.920 --> 01:01:58.710
It was...

01:01:59.380 --> 01:02:01.380
I haven't said anything yet.

01:02:01.460 --> 01:02:05.930
You were about to say something
stupid. I read your mind.

01:02:06.050 --> 01:02:09.390
According to your story,
you're not a psychic.

01:02:09.470 --> 01:02:13.310
I'm not.
So it's a mystery, isn't it?

01:02:15.390 --> 01:02:18.560
I'm going to go home.

01:02:18.650 --> 01:02:21.150
Isn't it dangerous?
You can...

01:02:21.230 --> 01:02:23.440
Sleep over?!
Are you serious?!

01:02:23.570 --> 01:02:27.110
Thanks but I'm fine.
I'm glad you're okay, Natsuki.

01:02:27.450 --> 01:02:28.740
I'll take you home.

01:02:28.820 --> 01:02:30.160
Me too.

01:02:30.240 --> 01:02:31.530
You're in your pajamas.

01:02:31.620 --> 01:02:33.200
Give me five minutes.

01:02:34.200 --> 01:02:38.250
Stop using the window!
And take your pillow!

01:03:07.780 --> 01:03:12.780
I feel better now. I should vent
my feelings sometimes too.

01:03:12.870 --> 01:03:15.790
You're always venting.

01:03:15.910 --> 01:03:18.420
No. I never do.

01:03:18.500 --> 01:03:20.210
Then you should.

01:03:23.800 --> 01:03:28.050
I won't be responsible for what
happens when I vent.

01:03:32.970 --> 01:03:34.560
Natsuki...

01:03:36.470 --> 01:03:38.640
Come to school.

01:03:39.140 --> 01:03:44.480
I don't know how Kyogoku and the
others want to change the world.

01:03:44.610 --> 01:03:47.490
But I want our lives
to be normal.

01:03:47.570 --> 01:03:51.240
We've always been
together, haven't we?

01:03:55.490 --> 01:03:57.410
That's not your line.

01:03:59.330 --> 01:04:00.960
It's not your line!

01:04:06.000 --> 01:04:07.340
Natsuki...

01:04:12.010 --> 01:04:15.260
I can worry if I want.

01:04:16.180 --> 01:04:17.520
Jerk.

01:04:18.600 --> 01:04:22.270
How did Kaho turn you down?

01:04:22.350 --> 01:04:24.650
You're asking me now?

01:04:24.730 --> 01:04:27.360
Tell me and
I'll go to school.

01:04:29.780 --> 01:04:33.450
Okay, fine, whatever.

01:04:53.840 --> 01:04:57.430
Are you okay?

01:04:57.890 --> 01:05:00.890
Mr. Open Fly.

01:05:01.140 --> 01:05:03.980
But you promised, okay?

01:05:05.730 --> 01:05:08.820
Bring your mobile
if you're worried.

01:05:09.150 --> 01:05:11.900
I'll bring mine too.

01:05:17.580 --> 01:05:18.910
What the...?

01:05:38.180 --> 01:05:40.640
There. I vented.

01:05:42.180 --> 01:05:44.350
I know how it feels.

01:05:44.940 --> 01:05:48.360
When you like someone
who likes someone else

01:05:48.940 --> 01:05:51.860
it's hard to show your feelings.

01:05:52.280 --> 01:05:54.860
And you want to know
how that person feels

01:05:55.610 --> 01:06:01.700
and you like that person
so much that it hurts.

01:06:06.290 --> 01:06:07.880
Because...

01:06:11.460 --> 01:06:14.130
Because I feel that way too.

01:06:16.260 --> 01:06:17.800
So don't, okay?

01:06:18.800 --> 01:06:24.180
Don't say I don't understand
how you feel!

01:06:40.240 --> 01:06:43.080
Even teachers can't
bring mobiles?

01:06:43.450 --> 01:06:45.120
No. It's the rule.

01:06:45.500 --> 01:06:49.170
Are teachers going to
get suspended too?

01:06:49.580 --> 01:06:51.590
That's the rule.

01:06:51.840 --> 01:06:54.510
Mr. Saito, please come here.

01:06:54.630 --> 01:06:56.380
Yes, Vice Principal?

01:06:56.510 --> 01:06:58.930
May I speak to you
in private?

01:07:05.180 --> 01:07:07.270
Good morning, Natsuki.

01:07:08.350 --> 01:07:10.190
When someone breaks
the rule...

01:07:10.270 --> 01:07:14.190
I'm disappointed you
ignored my warning.

01:07:15.190 --> 01:07:20.200
I waited because
he likes you and Kenji

01:07:20.280 --> 01:07:23.030
but I find it hard to understand.

01:07:23.160 --> 01:07:25.750
What did you do to
Jinno and Kondo?

01:07:25.870 --> 01:07:30.790
They're staying home. That's why
we're helping the council.

01:07:38.720 --> 01:07:42.890
You're not as perceptive
as I thought you were.

01:07:42.970 --> 01:07:46.390
Many people without the
power are cooperative.

01:07:46.520 --> 01:07:51.600
Like the vice principal. He's very
sympathetic with what we're doing.

01:07:52.060 --> 01:07:56.820
So we're making proposals to
make this a better school.

01:08:13.080 --> 01:08:16.840
Whoa... People can be so cruel.

01:08:22.760 --> 01:08:24.260
Ouch...

01:08:25.890 --> 01:08:27.140
Natsuki...

01:08:27.930 --> 01:08:30.520
People are watching.

01:08:48.120 --> 01:08:48.950
Natsuki...

01:08:49.620 --> 01:08:50.790
Get off.

01:08:51.460 --> 01:08:54.130
We have to climb the stairs.

01:08:55.710 --> 01:08:59.050
Um... Listen...

01:08:59.460 --> 01:09:02.300
I can feel your breasts.

01:09:05.970 --> 01:09:07.220
Pervert.

01:09:07.310 --> 01:09:08.970
Whatever.

01:09:09.100 --> 01:09:11.350
You like Kaho.

01:09:11.480 --> 01:09:12.890
Whatever.

01:09:12.980 --> 01:09:14.690
You don't care who, right?

01:09:14.810 --> 01:09:16.150
Give me a break.

01:09:16.230 --> 01:09:18.570
And you?
You don't care either?

01:09:20.820 --> 01:09:22.150
Sorry.

01:09:22.400 --> 01:09:25.110
Wear these.
Your feet are bleeding.

01:09:26.320 --> 01:09:28.910
What a tough
first day back.

01:09:29.080 --> 01:09:30.750
And tomorrow?

01:09:31.250 --> 01:09:32.040
How about you?

01:09:32.500 --> 01:09:33.330
Me?

01:09:33.410 --> 01:09:34.830
I'm going.

01:09:34.960 --> 01:09:35.790
Then I'll go.

01:09:47.930 --> 01:09:50.100
You shouldn't get too involved.

01:09:51.100 --> 01:09:53.690
Didn't one of my friends warn you?

01:09:55.850 --> 01:09:57.690
Why worry about me?

01:10:01.860 --> 01:10:06.780
People, when in a group, will
start a riot for small reasons.

01:10:06.860 --> 01:10:10.080
There's something
I want to ask you.

01:10:10.870 --> 01:10:12.370
You know everything.

01:10:13.200 --> 01:10:18.040
No, I don't. I don't know
what goes on in your mind.

01:10:18.130 --> 01:10:20.590
Because I don't
have the power?

01:10:26.470 --> 01:10:27.720
That's right.

01:10:30.890 --> 01:10:35.640
In the future, humankind doesn't
live on Earth anymore.

01:10:36.230 --> 01:10:37.230
What?

01:10:37.900 --> 01:10:42.480
People's behavior exceeded
the limit of Earth's endurance.

01:10:43.070 --> 01:10:45.490
Humans can't live on it anymore.

01:10:45.900 --> 01:10:47.860
So we live on the moon.

01:10:49.910 --> 01:10:52.830
See? That's my homeland.

01:10:53.490 --> 01:10:55.410
It feels so bizarre.

01:10:55.540 --> 01:10:59.130
Looking up at the moon from Earth.

01:11:01.250 --> 01:11:04.670
<i>It happened one day
without warning.</i>

01:11:05.340 --> 01:11:09.510
<i>Only a spaceship that was
away from Earth survived.</i>

01:11:10.600 --> 01:11:15.600
<i>We discovered Earth needed
1,000 years to become livable again.</i>

01:11:16.430 --> 01:11:20.270
<i>We didn't have the technology
nor the resources</i>

01:11:20.350 --> 01:11:22.400
<i>to survive so many years.</i>

01:11:25.440 --> 01:11:28.780
<i>Humans will never
return to Earth.</i>

01:11:32.280 --> 01:11:34.200
Time passed.

01:11:34.450 --> 01:11:38.620
Some children started
displaying a strange ability.

01:11:39.120 --> 01:11:41.040
A Psychic power?

01:11:41.130 --> 01:11:44.090
That's what you call it.

01:11:44.170 --> 01:11:48.380
Most areas of the human brain
are dormant most of the time.

01:11:49.130 --> 01:11:53.640
An unfamiliar power could be
awakened in a crisis.

01:11:54.510 --> 01:11:56.310
That's what some believe.

01:11:59.810 --> 01:12:02.310
<i>Nobody knows for sure.</i>

01:12:02.400 --> 01:12:07.490
<i>But in our era, this is
none other than hope.</i>

01:12:07.610 --> 01:12:08.650
<i>Hope?</i>

01:12:08.780 --> 01:12:14.660
<i>Yeah. People probably can't
stand not doing anything.</i>

01:12:15.160 --> 01:12:18.500
<i>We need hope to stay alive.</i>

01:12:20.080 --> 01:12:23.670
<i>The power is awakened
around the age of 14.</i>

01:12:25.090 --> 01:12:29.170
<i>Around the time when you first
start feeling self-conscious</i>

01:12:29.300 --> 01:12:32.130
<i>or confused and anguished
about relationships.</i>

01:12:32.340 --> 01:12:34.510
<i>The two periods
might be related.</i>

01:12:34.600 --> 01:12:38.850
<i>Some say this power
could prevent conflict.</i>

01:12:39.020 --> 01:12:45.190
<i>My mission is to awaken as many
power users as possible in this era.</i>

01:12:46.690 --> 01:12:50.700
<i>That way, we may be able
to prevent that disaster.</i>

01:12:51.700 --> 01:12:55.950
If not, I have to bring back
power users to my era.

01:12:57.540 --> 01:13:02.290
In my era, human population
is very small.

01:13:02.540 --> 01:13:05.380
Even a smaller population
of power users.

01:13:06.210 --> 01:13:09.380
We fight those who
stand in our way.

01:13:10.550 --> 01:13:13.590
Even if it's you or Kenji...

01:13:14.510 --> 01:13:15.930
<i>Or anyone else.</i>

01:13:18.100 --> 01:13:23.060
<i>So if this is “A Midsummer
Night's Dream,” I'm Puck.</i>

01:13:24.060 --> 01:13:27.060
I'm here to put a magic
spell on humans.

01:13:31.190 --> 01:13:33.030
Why are you telling me?

01:13:37.120 --> 01:13:38.410
I...

01:13:40.240 --> 01:13:42.830
I don't know what to do.

01:13:58.220 --> 01:14:02.270
Sometimes fairies fall
in love with humans.

01:14:03.310 --> 01:14:06.020
You know a story like that?

01:14:08.440 --> 01:14:13.530
Or maybe I put a spell on myself.

01:14:15.280 --> 01:14:17.950
Puck is a prankster after all.

01:14:19.780 --> 01:14:22.620
<i>I'll count to three.</i>

01:14:22.700 --> 01:14:26.040
<i>And when I clap my hands</i>

01:14:26.120 --> 01:14:31.420
<i>you'll forget everything and
wake up feeling refreshed.</i>

01:14:31.880 --> 01:14:35.590
<i>Three, two, one.</i>

01:14:35.680 --> 01:14:36.720
<i>Now!</i>

01:14:45.480 --> 01:14:47.810
<i>If this is a magic spell...</i>

01:14:48.980 --> 01:14:53.320
<i>I don't want it to end.</i>

01:15:07.160 --> 01:15:10.670
<i>My mother was born in this era.</i>

01:15:12.840 --> 01:15:14.920
<i>I have no recollection of her.</i>

01:15:15.010 --> 01:15:18.840
<i>They say she died right
after I was born.</i>

01:15:20.760 --> 01:15:22.180
<i>No photographs of her.</i>

01:15:23.510 --> 01:15:25.390
<i>Record of the past are worthless.</i>

01:15:25.520 --> 01:15:29.810
<i>What's important is the future.
That's what my father believes.</i>

01:15:32.520 --> 01:15:37.610
<i>Still, a few of my mother's
belongings were left behind.</i>

01:15:38.990 --> 01:15:41.320
<i>Secretly looking at them</i>

01:15:41.620 --> 01:15:46.160
<i>was my private, childhood pastime.</i>

01:15:55.130 --> 01:15:56.340
<i>Kaho, come!</i>

01:15:56.630 --> 01:15:58.420
Natsuki's in trouble!

01:16:02.140 --> 01:16:04.850
You can't just
open my locker.

01:16:04.930 --> 01:16:10.390
Natsuki Suzuura, you are
suspended for 10 days.

01:16:10.480 --> 01:16:15.070
The next time, 30 days.
The third time, 90 days.

01:16:15.190 --> 01:16:16.030
Give it back.

01:16:16.110 --> 01:16:17.650
Let go of it.

01:16:17.740 --> 01:16:19.070
Stop it.

01:16:19.200 --> 01:16:20.280
Give it back!

01:16:25.660 --> 01:16:27.910
I can walk by myself!

01:16:28.250 --> 01:16:30.750
Go! Faster!

01:16:31.250 --> 01:16:32.670
Let me get changed!

01:16:38.760 --> 01:16:39.470
Come on!

01:16:39.590 --> 01:16:40.510
Go!

01:16:40.590 --> 01:16:42.220
You can do it!

01:16:42.590 --> 01:16:44.600
Let go of me!

01:16:46.260 --> 01:16:47.680
Are you sure?

01:16:48.520 --> 01:16:52.190
My father wants to release
Kenji's power, doesn't he?

01:16:55.610 --> 01:16:59.030
Is he still trying?

01:16:59.190 --> 01:17:00.610
Go on.

01:17:01.360 --> 01:17:03.360
To your master.

01:17:06.950 --> 01:17:11.620
<i>The one who decides how to use
the power is not me nor you.</i>

01:17:11.710 --> 01:17:13.960
<i>Tell that to your father.</i>

01:17:14.750 --> 01:17:17.750
Tell him to leave
the past alone.

01:17:18.460 --> 01:17:20.510
Why are mobile phones forbidden?

01:17:21.130 --> 01:17:23.380
I'm coming to school tomorrow.

01:17:24.800 --> 01:17:26.550
I promised.

01:17:26.800 --> 01:17:30.220
I don't understand
what you're saying.

01:17:30.310 --> 01:17:35.100
Forgive me for not being able
to use telepathy like you.

01:17:35.310 --> 01:17:39.570
Why don't you forbid talking
and listening too?

01:17:39.650 --> 01:17:40.650
What's your point?

01:17:40.780 --> 01:17:44.200
You just want to pretend
to know the answer.

01:17:44.320 --> 01:17:46.990
Reading people's minds?

01:17:47.120 --> 01:17:49.080
That's like peeping.

01:17:49.490 --> 01:17:54.250
Wanting to tell, wanting to know...
That's what counts.

01:17:54.330 --> 01:17:56.670
Peeping?
How dare you!

01:17:56.790 --> 01:18:01.380
If you don't want to tell your
feelings, they'll never get through.

01:18:01.510 --> 01:18:05.680
People who don't want to
understand won't understand.

01:18:06.140 --> 01:18:09.350
It's not about mobile phones
or telepathy.

01:18:09.640 --> 01:18:11.470
It's necessary in the future.

01:18:11.560 --> 01:18:16.060
I don't care about the future!
We're living in the present!

01:18:16.190 --> 01:18:18.480
Shut up if you're
not going to fight.

01:18:19.060 --> 01:18:20.520
It's people like you...

01:18:20.610 --> 01:18:23.690
You're the one
who's not fighting.

01:18:45.880 --> 01:18:49.640
What? We had swimming.

01:18:50.760 --> 01:18:54.770
A mobile?
I brought mine too.

01:19:07.110 --> 01:19:09.240
Are you gonna
confiscate it too?

01:19:13.990 --> 01:19:16.250
<i>What was my mother like?</i>

01:19:16.370 --> 01:19:18.920
<i>Don't you use telepathy?</i>

01:19:19.750 --> 01:19:23.000
I want to hear it said
in your words.

01:19:24.840 --> 01:19:28.430
All right.
She was a beautiful woman.

01:19:28.680 --> 01:19:30.550
You two look alike.

01:19:30.930 --> 01:19:32.680
So I've been told.

01:19:33.430 --> 01:19:36.850
She had her own beliefs.

01:19:36.930 --> 01:19:40.940
To tell you the truth,
I had a crush on her.

01:19:42.020 --> 01:19:45.780
I hoped she'd be
happy in the future.

01:19:46.690 --> 01:19:49.320
Do you think she was happy?

01:19:52.120 --> 01:19:55.870
I was hoping you'd tell me.

01:20:02.790 --> 01:20:06.010
Wait, Kenji! Wait!

01:20:22.810 --> 01:20:24.980
I'm going now.

01:20:25.480 --> 01:20:26.480
All right.

01:20:28.650 --> 01:20:30.820
What are you going to do?

01:20:31.490 --> 01:20:32.950
About what?

01:20:33.030 --> 01:20:36.580
Half of your blood
is from this era.

01:20:38.250 --> 01:20:41.710
Couldn't you stay and
live in this era?

01:20:49.170 --> 01:20:54.260
I think people are happiest living
in the era they were born in.

01:20:54.760 --> 01:20:58.680
I was sure you'd say that.

01:21:00.180 --> 01:21:01.640
You're right.

01:21:02.520 --> 01:21:05.440
<i>It was a stupid question.</i>

01:21:17.530 --> 01:21:19.620
You hold it, you pervert!

01:21:20.330 --> 01:21:22.250
Where are you putting it?

01:21:22.370 --> 01:21:24.880
The only pocket is in here.

01:21:25.000 --> 01:21:26.840
Give me mine!

01:21:26.920 --> 01:21:28.420
Okay, fine.

01:21:28.550 --> 01:21:31.970
No! That's not a pocket!

01:21:35.140 --> 01:21:38.680
I told you you're a psychic.

01:21:39.100 --> 01:21:41.560
Yeah. It seems so.

01:21:42.480 --> 01:21:44.400
Let's finish this.

01:21:44.900 --> 01:21:47.480
This is our fate.

01:21:50.150 --> 01:21:52.150
Hey, you know what?

01:21:52.820 --> 01:21:54.660
Tomorrow's the weekend.

01:21:56.320 --> 01:21:57.240
So?

01:21:57.370 --> 01:21:59.120
Wanna go to the beach?

01:22:05.750 --> 01:22:06.670
Huh?

01:22:14.010 --> 01:22:17.010
<i>The typhoon that
developed on the 4th</i>

01:22:17.090 --> 01:22:20.430
<i>traveled over the
Ogasawara Islands</i>

01:22:20.560 --> 01:22:26.310
<i>and is moving southeast 200 km
off the shores of Chichijima...</i>

01:22:29.900 --> 01:22:33.400
Don't you have any common sense?

01:22:34.150 --> 01:22:37.740
Why are we at the beach
in this weather?

01:22:37.820 --> 01:22:39.160
Why not?
It's summer.

01:22:39.280 --> 01:22:41.200
But...!

01:22:41.290 --> 01:22:42.910
It <i>is</i> summer.

01:22:44.290 --> 01:22:47.120
I feel like a worry wart.

01:22:47.620 --> 01:22:49.590
It'll be sunny later.

01:22:49.960 --> 01:22:53.460
That really wasn't my point.

01:22:53.550 --> 01:22:55.800
Hey... I brought the script.

01:22:55.920 --> 01:22:56.930
The play?

01:22:57.010 --> 01:22:58.180
Let's practice.

01:22:58.300 --> 01:22:59.050
Yeah, let's.

01:22:59.140 --> 01:22:59.850
You're kidding.

01:22:59.970 --> 01:23:02.720
I brought lunch.
Which first?

01:23:02.810 --> 01:23:05.270
I didn't know you
were so adaptable.

01:23:05.350 --> 01:23:06.520
I say lunch!

01:23:06.640 --> 01:23:08.400
Natsuki made lunch
for you.

01:23:09.980 --> 01:23:11.980
Don't be rude.

01:23:12.070 --> 01:23:13.940
I might pass out.

01:23:14.030 --> 01:23:16.820
Rude? Pass out?

01:23:16.900 --> 01:23:18.240
I was just...

01:23:18.320 --> 01:23:20.530
Let's all eat together.

01:23:31.340 --> 01:23:33.420
You guys! You're kidding.

01:23:54.780 --> 01:23:57.440
Sorry to make you
worry all the time.

01:23:59.030 --> 01:24:00.200
Who are you?

01:24:00.700 --> 01:24:02.200
Kenji is...

01:24:02.620 --> 01:24:05.040
That's me.
I died that day.

01:24:08.620 --> 01:24:13.000
But you slipped back in time
and got hurt in my place

01:24:13.590 --> 01:24:15.340
and lost the power.

01:24:16.050 --> 01:24:21.390
When you change something,
something else changes for balance.

01:24:26.970 --> 01:24:28.890
Take care.

01:24:29.890 --> 01:24:31.310
Are you going somewhere?

01:24:31.400 --> 01:24:34.110
Wait! Stop!

01:24:38.570 --> 01:24:41.910
Don't go! You promised!

01:24:42.910 --> 01:24:48.830
We're always going to stay
next to each other, aren't we?

01:24:50.410 --> 01:24:52.170
<i>Liar.</i>

01:24:53.920 --> 01:24:56.130
Don't go!

01:24:57.750 --> 01:24:58.920
<i>Kenji...</i>

01:24:59.050 --> 01:25:00.920
You promised.

01:25:01.300 --> 01:25:01.930
<i>Kenji...</i>

01:25:02.010 --> 01:25:04.390
You said so yourself.

01:25:04.760 --> 01:25:08.770
You said we'll always
stay next to each other.

01:25:12.770 --> 01:25:14.350
<i>Kenji...</i>

01:25:17.440 --> 01:25:18.860
<i>You jerk.</i>

01:25:21.030 --> 01:25:22.360
<i>Jerk...</i>

01:25:34.830 --> 01:25:36.710
The sun came out.

01:25:38.460 --> 01:25:41.970
Was I saying something?

01:25:48.720 --> 01:25:50.970
You know now.

01:25:52.140 --> 01:25:56.310
Actually I've known for a long time.

01:25:57.560 --> 01:25:59.150
Since when?

01:25:59.270 --> 01:26:04.200
You came to school every day
because of Kenji.

01:26:04.990 --> 01:26:07.660
I realized how much
you like him.

01:26:12.000 --> 01:26:14.710
But Kenji likes you, Kaho.

01:26:17.750 --> 01:26:19.500
It's not fair.

01:26:20.090 --> 01:26:22.920
I liked him first.

01:26:24.010 --> 01:26:25.510
For so long...

01:26:28.180 --> 01:26:30.100
I've liked him.

01:26:30.430 --> 01:26:32.350
For so long...

01:26:33.100 --> 01:26:35.190
It's not fair.

01:26:43.440 --> 01:26:47.200
So your dad knew my grandpa?

01:26:48.280 --> 01:26:49.950
They weren't friends.

01:26:50.780 --> 01:26:55.460
When my dad came to this era,
your grandpa got in his way.

01:26:55.790 --> 01:26:57.790
Why didn't he come with you?

01:26:57.870 --> 01:27:00.750
You can time travel only once.

01:27:00.880 --> 01:27:03.050
It's bad for the heart.

01:27:04.130 --> 01:27:06.720
I sense his presence sometimes.

01:27:07.720 --> 01:27:09.050
You do?

01:27:10.300 --> 01:27:11.300
You do, huh?

01:27:14.810 --> 01:27:16.230
I'll get you back!

01:27:20.230 --> 01:27:23.280
I've come to like acting.

01:27:23.610 --> 01:27:24.480
Yeah?

01:27:24.990 --> 01:27:27.900
It's nice talking like this.

01:27:28.910 --> 01:27:30.740
Talking is acting?

01:27:30.820 --> 01:27:33.740
Because you don't let
me read your mind.

01:27:34.240 --> 01:27:37.660
Your power is stronger
than mine by far.

01:27:37.910 --> 01:27:42.000
Like the sun and the moon.
That's why it's a one-way street.

01:27:43.170 --> 01:27:46.300
You can't see moonlight
during the day.

01:27:47.300 --> 01:27:50.510
Even though the moon
is out during the day.

01:27:50.930 --> 01:27:53.600
What's taking you guys so long?

01:28:12.990 --> 01:28:17.000
Oh my God... This is scary.

01:28:17.120 --> 01:28:19.040
Really scary!

01:28:22.960 --> 01:28:25.550
Ouch!

01:28:25.630 --> 01:28:26.590
Here we go.

01:28:26.880 --> 01:28:29.300
Get closer.

01:28:39.770 --> 01:28:41.810
<i>So this is summer.</i>

01:28:42.190 --> 01:28:45.320
<i>Oh... You don't have the seasons.</i>

01:28:45.650 --> 01:28:46.690
<i>No.</i>

01:28:50.400 --> 01:28:52.570
<i>In “A Midsummer Night's Dream”</i>

01:28:52.860 --> 01:28:57.490
<i>they forget their dreams
when they wake up, right?</i>

01:28:57.990 --> 01:28:59.790
<i>Why? Suddenly...</i>

01:29:00.000 --> 01:29:02.420
<i>It's like hypnosis.</i>

01:29:02.830 --> 01:29:03.960
<i>But...</i>

01:29:06.290 --> 01:29:10.970
If you fall in love
under a magic spell...

01:29:13.720 --> 01:29:17.350
When you wake up from the spell

01:29:17.890 --> 01:29:21.690
and if that love you felt
in the dream disappears

01:29:22.690 --> 01:29:27.440
where does that feeling of love go?

01:29:32.570 --> 01:29:36.530
I have to go back to the moon.

01:29:37.240 --> 01:29:40.450
Go back? When?

01:29:41.040 --> 01:29:43.370
Tonight, I think.

01:29:45.290 --> 01:29:48.920
Then you'll probably forget about me.

01:29:49.960 --> 01:29:52.050
Like “A Midsummer Night's Dream.”

01:29:54.300 --> 01:29:57.640
This is full already.

01:29:57.890 --> 01:29:59.310
Full?

01:29:59.510 --> 01:30:02.930
Full to the top with time.

01:30:03.850 --> 01:30:07.810
With the several months
that I've been gone.

01:30:12.030 --> 01:30:17.070
<i>Goodbye. I wish I could have
listened to your “Moonlight.”</i>

01:30:23.790 --> 01:30:27.960
Puck is such a prankster
but a lovable one.

01:30:28.080 --> 01:30:30.340
What are you talking about?

01:30:30.420 --> 01:30:32.380
He's probably serious.

01:30:33.010 --> 01:30:35.090
Playing pranks aren't nice.

01:30:35.220 --> 01:30:37.010
We don't know
what he's thinking.

01:30:37.760 --> 01:30:39.970
<i>What goes on in
fairies' minds...</i>

01:30:47.600 --> 01:30:49.270
Don't go.

01:30:50.690 --> 01:30:52.860
I have to.

01:30:52.940 --> 01:30:54.570
I like you so much.

01:30:55.530 --> 01:30:57.950
Really, I do.

01:31:00.240 --> 01:31:03.120
I could never forget you.

01:31:04.370 --> 01:31:05.870
If you're going...

01:31:05.960 --> 01:31:07.000
No.

01:31:07.120 --> 01:31:09.460
If you're going, then...

01:31:09.540 --> 01:31:10.790
No!

01:31:14.880 --> 01:31:16.260
I'll...

01:31:19.390 --> 01:31:21.600
I'll go with you.

01:31:27.480 --> 01:31:28.900
Let's go.

01:31:29.310 --> 01:31:30.650
Go where?

01:31:30.730 --> 01:31:31.820
Get on.

01:31:31.940 --> 01:31:37.110
Without you, there'll be nothing
to keep me in this era.

01:31:39.320 --> 01:31:40.280
What?

01:31:42.280 --> 01:31:43.490
I won't repeat it.

01:31:43.620 --> 01:31:45.450
What did you say?

01:31:45.540 --> 01:31:46.160
Come on.

01:31:46.250 --> 01:31:48.250
Say it again, meanie.

01:31:52.500 --> 01:31:53.840
Sorry.

01:31:59.340 --> 01:32:03.350
My mother was from this era.

01:32:04.510 --> 01:32:07.600
When she came to the future

01:32:08.020 --> 01:32:11.190
she was probably lonely,
very lonely.

01:32:30.170 --> 01:32:31.420
Good bye.

01:33:06.740 --> 01:33:07.790
Hey.

01:33:10.960 --> 01:33:12.120
You alone?

01:33:12.460 --> 01:33:13.460
Yeah.

01:33:14.250 --> 01:33:15.590
I see.

01:33:22.510 --> 01:33:25.430
I came to see you off.

01:33:25.550 --> 01:33:26.930
When you leave...

01:33:28.770 --> 01:33:30.230
I'll break this.

01:33:32.270 --> 01:33:34.730
I can't allow that.

01:33:51.790 --> 01:33:53.960
I don't want to fight you.

01:33:54.080 --> 01:33:56.420
You won't exist in
this world anymore.

01:33:56.500 --> 01:33:59.050
It's okay.
It's my mission.

01:34:36.670 --> 01:34:40.420
Ryoichi, get rid of them.
Get their power!

01:34:41.000 --> 01:34:44.920
Then the future will change.
Humankind will survive.

01:34:45.010 --> 01:34:47.180
Survive and then what?

01:34:47.260 --> 01:34:48.300
What?

01:34:49.010 --> 01:34:52.850
A past that has no
future won't change.

01:34:53.850 --> 01:34:55.020
We've done enough.

01:34:55.100 --> 01:34:58.520
You fool. Your theory is wrong.

01:34:58.650 --> 01:35:03.110
Why? I know you
already know... Dad.

01:35:05.400 --> 01:35:11.410
Because you couldn't
return Mom to this era.

01:35:14.540 --> 01:35:17.210
You have me.

01:35:18.540 --> 01:35:22.000
Me, who's not supposed to exist.

01:35:30.600 --> 01:35:31.300
No!

01:35:32.390 --> 01:35:35.560
Why? Earth...

01:35:37.060 --> 01:35:40.400
Why does it keep rejecting us?

01:36:05.670 --> 01:36:07.340
<i>It's like snow.</i>

01:36:10.340 --> 01:36:14.850
<i>Wait... Have I ever seen snow?</i>

01:36:17.850 --> 01:36:22.270
<i>Ah... It must be from the stories
Mom told me</i>

01:36:22.440 --> 01:36:25.280
<i>when I was a kid.</i>

01:36:27.610 --> 01:36:28.360
Kenji!

01:36:28.440 --> 01:36:31.780
You used up your power
knowing this would happen.

01:36:31.910 --> 01:36:34.990
Go away...
You'll get drawn in too.

01:36:35.450 --> 01:36:39.870
<i>Kyogoku, your and my
hearts aren't connected.</i>

01:36:41.120 --> 01:36:43.960
But our hands can connect.

01:36:45.130 --> 01:36:46.710
Isn't that good enough?

01:36:47.710 --> 01:36:52.140
<i>Your hands are warm.
I can feel your heat.</i>

01:36:52.470 --> 01:36:54.220
Isn't that good enough?

01:37:23.080 --> 01:37:25.040
Kenji!

01:37:28.090 --> 01:37:29.090
Huh?

01:37:32.180 --> 01:37:34.680
What are you doing?

01:37:35.090 --> 01:37:38.770
I told you I came
to see you off.

01:37:38.850 --> 01:37:43.140
I can't exist in this era anymore.

01:37:43.560 --> 01:37:46.860
I can't go back.
I'll disappear soon.

01:37:46.980 --> 01:37:48.780
I'll take you.

01:37:49.690 --> 01:37:52.450
I can manage a
one-way trip.

01:37:52.740 --> 01:37:55.740
Don't be stupid.
You'll be stuck.

01:37:56.120 --> 01:37:57.780
Kyogoku...

01:37:58.700 --> 01:38:01.500
Nobody is “not supposed to exist.”

01:38:02.870 --> 01:38:08.540
You still exist here because there
are people who want you here.

01:38:09.880 --> 01:38:13.050
Me... You...

01:38:13.630 --> 01:38:17.680
Maybe everybody.

01:38:24.980 --> 01:38:27.360
Maybe you're right.

01:38:30.230 --> 01:38:31.780
Sorry, Natsuki.

01:38:33.240 --> 01:38:35.150
I'll be right back.

01:38:35.240 --> 01:38:37.030
Where are you going?

01:38:37.120 --> 01:38:38.740
Wait for me.

01:38:38.950 --> 01:38:41.040
You want me to wait?

01:38:42.830 --> 01:38:43.910
Yeah.

01:38:44.040 --> 01:38:45.500
If...

01:38:45.920 --> 01:38:48.420
If I was born in this era

01:38:48.750 --> 01:38:50.420
we could have been...

01:38:50.500 --> 01:38:52.090
Shut up.

01:38:53.920 --> 01:38:58.340
The you I know was our friend.

01:38:59.600 --> 01:39:02.270
No matter how many
light years we're apart

01:39:02.930 --> 01:39:04.770
that won't change.

01:39:23.700 --> 01:39:24.950
Kenji!

01:39:54.730 --> 01:39:56.190
Kenji?

01:40:00.200 --> 01:40:02.160
What was I doing?

01:40:10.370 --> 01:40:12.340
Kenji...

01:40:16.090 --> 01:40:17.760
Who's that?

01:44:45.480 --> 01:44:46.980
Did you hear?

01:44:47.110 --> 01:44:47.860
About what?

01:44:47.940 --> 01:44:50.240
The new student.

01:44:50.650 --> 01:44:52.280
New student?

01:45:02.170 --> 01:45:03.830
I don't know this number.

01:45:10.340 --> 01:45:14.050
Will you please answer
your mobile?

01:45:19.350 --> 01:45:22.060
That's weird...

01:45:22.310 --> 01:45:26.650
This was supposed to make
you remember me.

01:45:42.830 --> 01:45:44.290
Jerk...

01:45:49.000 --> 01:45:50.170
Natsuki?

01:45:50.630 --> 01:45:51.800
You're a jerk!

01:45:57.720 --> 01:45:59.180
I'm back.

01:46:01.890 --> 01:46:03.270
<i>Jerk.</i>

01:46:06.060 --> 01:46:11.110
Directed by      Ryosuke Nakamura

01:46:13.820 --> 01:46:19.740
The End

